Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Use ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["TensorNetworkQ",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/TensorNetworkQ"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"6973dcb1-c814-4cea-a25a-788db420bd91"],
 " to test whether an expression is a valid network. It checks both the head \
and the structural invariants (lengths agree, every hyperedge length equals \
the rank of its tensor, every output leg is a label that actually appears). \
Predicates of this form are useful as guards inside ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["PatternTest",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/PatternTest"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"b432653c-d662-46a6-b180-dd64bccab017"],
 " constructions."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7145166b-7de3-4a6d-b93d-652b8c5089af"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TensorNetworkQ", "[", "tn", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:=",ExpressionUUID->"06e5ae0e-4045-4cb7-8950-ade1e938d48d"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9880587805630217`*^9, 3.988065094612356*^9, 
  3.988112652415092*^9, 3.988113452812171*^9, 3.988115546949278*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[9]=",
 CellID->1963702458,ExpressionUUID->"4a460492-dcac-4153-a906-968127164db9"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The free indices are the ones that appear in exactly one hyperedge \
\[LongDash] the network's open legs. When the output specification is ",
 StyleBox["Automatic", "Code"],
 ", the free-index list is computed automatically by counting label \
occurrences. The next section shows how to override that to expose contracted \
legs or to scalar-out."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0638d88e-40f1-4c90-8c78-3a43269b1c72"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"tn", "[", "\"\<FreeIndices\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:=",ExpressionUUID->"cd7d9bab-9e62-4039-b1ae-4da3657e6d33"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"1", ",", "3"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.988058782703391*^9, 3.988065094629532*^9, 
  3.9881126524289713`*^9, 3.9881134528217*^9, 3.9881155469630404`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[10]=",
 CellID->1418524510,ExpressionUUID->"132ce779-0c1e-4916-8b03-c14c7630bd44"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. Constructor forms", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"cb26a885-ff9b-431e-b76e-de18f94c643f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "There are four idiomatic ways to construct a network. The first three start \
from existing tensors \[LongDash] either fully numeric or carrying symbolic \
entries \[LongDash] and differ only in the syntax used to attach them to a \
hypergraph. The fourth bypasses tensors entirely: you describe the shape of \
the network with a hypergraph and a dimension association, and the \
constructor populates each slot with an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["ArraySymbol",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/ArraySymbol"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"ff5a02fc-0e29-4dd2-aaa0-2ebdf9e8d223"],
 " placeholder of the correct rank and dimensions. The symbolic form is \
useful for planning a contraction before the numerics exist, for index-only \
analyses, and for testing path search under specific shape regimes."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b0b1ed02-7c27-4b61-a929-453c43999263"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2.1. Tensors plus a hyperedge list", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"a285b735-eac5-45be-8a81-895cb6bea03d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Form 1: tensors plus a hyperedge list. Each inner list is one hyperedge, \
naming the legs it joins. The constructor matches the leg names to tensor \
ranks in order \[LongDash] the ",
 StyleBox["k", "Code"],
 "th label inside the ",
 StyleBox["i", "Code"],
 "th hyperedge corresponds to the ",
 StyleBox["k", "Code"],
 "th axis of the ",
 StyleBox["i", "Code"],
 "th tensor. Shapes must match: if the same label appears twice, the two \
corresponding tensor axes must have the same dimension."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.988058915118552*^9, 
  3.988058916338851*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"882af3e5-896a-4a9e-a2d9-\
d9d0fa6f0f51"],

